  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Lotze et son héritage (2015), published by Peter Lang Verlag, has been cited 4 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Lotze et son héritage by Federico Boccaccini was published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2015. It is part of the Philosophie et Politique / Philosophy and Politics series. Conceptually, the work connects to Art.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 4 citations. Citations peaked in 2017 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Klassische Texte der Wissenschaft, Les Cahiers philosophiques de Strasbourg and Hermann eBooks. The citing works include 2 journal articles and 2 book chapters. They come from 3 countries, led by Chile, Germany and France.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It is recorded in 4 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
